    "unit": "currency/year",
    "threshold_unit": null,
    "label": {
      "en": "Limit complementary pension insurance, from 2014"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tscsepi_uplim"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "$tscsepi_uplim (currency/year, latest €44,286) defines the annual income ceiling of the first (lower-rate) band of the complementary old-age pension contribution schedule for self-employed industry-and-trade workers, in force since 2014 per its label. It is used as the Band_UpLim parameter in tscse_fr/SchedCalc's 'I&T: Complementary pension insurance contributions for industry & trade' function — the same function that uses $tscsepi_industry_rate8 as its Band_Rate — marking the point up to which that lower rate applies, consistent with the Country Report's description of this contribution as '7% of r<PSS, 8% of PSS<r<4×PSS' (tscse.md, Table 2.64). The figure does not equal $PSS's own value for the same period in the data reviewed, so this ceiling may be uprated on a somewhat different schedule than the general PSS; no source in this batch documents its exact derivation."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Parameters for self-employed contributions"
    },
    "last_confirmed_valid_on": null,
    "temporal_basis": "in_force"
  },
